  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 221 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nBy the beginning of the week, the slow moving surface high will be \nnearing the Ohio River Valley leading to the return of light \nsoutherly flow and continued airmass modification. Guidance is in \ngood agreement that 925mb temperatures should be near 5C for most of \nthe area on Monday and Tuesday. Complete mixing would result in high \ntemperatures mostly in the mid 50s each afternoon, which is near \nseasonal normals. Eventually, the surface high slides off into the \nMid Atlantic leading to the return of WAA thanks to stronger \nsoutherly flow. By the middle to late part of next week, there is \ngood agreement that seasonably warm temperatures return with highs \nback into the 60s across the area. Additionally, long-range guidance \nreveals longwave troughing across the Pacific Coast with a shortwave \ntraversing ahead of the main wave and into the Midwest late next \nweek. As a result, probabilities for 24hr measurable precipitation \nreach near 50% for most of the region by next Friday according to \nthe LREF. Until then, dry conditions are expected to continue into \nat least the middle of next week.",
